mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Prosthodontics is a clinical science that studies the application of physiological methods to repair various defects in the oral and maxillofacial region with artificial devices and restore their physiological functions, as well as prevent and treat diseases of the oral and maxillofacial system. It involves multiple disciplines such as oral clinical medicine, materials science, and aesthetics. It researches the causes, symptoms, diagnosis, and treatment methods of diseases related to the oral and maxillofacial system, and uses artificial materials to fabricate various devices or prostheses to restore, reconstruct, or correct various congenital or acquired defects or abnormalities of the oral and maxillofacial system in patients, thereby restoring normal morphology and function.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
